<h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Welsh-language and accessibility takeaway</h2>

<p class="govuk-body-l">
  Roughly <strong>538,000 people in Wales</strong> spoke Welsh in the 2021 ONS census (17.8% of the population aged 3+). The Welsh Government's <em>Cymraeg 2050</em> strategy targets a million Welsh speakers by 2050. UK councils with statutory Welsh-language duties cannot ship a residents-facing AI Contact Centre without parity.
</p>

<h3 class="govuk-heading-m">The AWS gap, today</h3>

<table class="govuk-table">
  <thead class="govuk-table__head">
    <tr class="govuk-table__row">
      <th scope="col" class="govuk-table__header">Capability</th>
      <th scope="col" class="govuk-table__header">English (en_GB) today</th>
      <th scope="col" class="govuk-table__header">Welsh (cy_GB) today</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody class="govuk-table__body">
    <tr class="govuk-table__row">
      <th scope="row" class="govuk-table__header">Real-time speech-to-text</th>
      <td class="govuk-table__cell">Amazon Transcribe streaming, Contact Lens-integrated</td>
      <td class="govuk-table__cell"><strong>Batch only.</strong> No streaming Transcribe for cy-WL.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr class="govuk-table__row">
      <th scope="row" class="govuk-table__header">Lex v2 NLU</th>
      <td class="govuk-table__cell">Full feature set, en_GB native</td>
      <td class="govuk-table__cell"><strong>Limited.</strong> cy_GB is feature-limited. Slot types and intent classifiers are not at parity.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr class="govuk-table__row">
      <th scope="row" class="govuk-table__header">Polly text-to-speech</th>
      <td class="govuk-table__cell">Neural en-GB (Amy, Brian, Arthur)</td>
      <td class="govuk-table__cell"><strong>Standard engine only.</strong> No Neural Welsh voice.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3 class="govuk-heading-m">Strategic ask</h3>

<p class="govuk-body">If you're a UK gov body procuring contact-centre AI, here are the four questions to put to your AWS Technical Account Manager:</p>

<ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number govuk-list--spaced">
  <li>What is the ETA for <strong>Welsh streaming Transcribe</strong>? What is the AWS roadmap commitment? Ask AWS TAM to put it in writing.</li>
  <li>What is the ETA for <strong>native cy_GB Lex NLU</strong> with parity to en_GB? What partial-parity milestones exist? Ask your AWS Technical Account Manager.</li>
  <li>What is the ETA for <strong>Polly Neural Welsh</strong>? Is there a generative-voice alternative? Ask AWS TAM.</li>
  <li>What is the AWS roadmap for <strong>BSL via video relay</strong>? Could a third-party integration meet a council's statutory equality duties? Ask your AWS Technical Account Manager what to ask AWS partners.</li>
</ol>

<h3 class="govuk-heading-m">Accessibility beyond Welsh</h3>

<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
  <li><strong>TTY support.</strong> Amazon Connect supports TTY for hearing-impaired callers via the standard PSTN path. No additional configuration in this scenario.</li>
  <li><strong>Live Transcription.</strong> Contact Lens's redacted transcript stream can be surfaced to a deaf or hearing-impaired caller's companion device in real time.</li>
  <li><strong>SMS reporting alternatives.</strong> For residents who can't or won't use voice, the same multimodal Lambda accepts a WhatsApp/SMS-equivalent payload. The Lambda code path is identical.</li>
  <li><strong>BSL via video relay.</strong> Outside this scenario today. Documented here so a procurement conversation with AWS TAM has a starting point.</li>
</ul>

